<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea May precious metals import prices down.</title>
<headline>S.Korea May precious metals import prices down.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's precious metals import prices went down in May from the previous month due to falling prices in world markets, the Association of Foreign Trading Agents of Korea (AFTAK) said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Import prices of precious metals were as follows:</p>
<p>(price per tonne on CIF)</p>
<p> METAL		  May	 Apr</p>
<p> Gold (gram)	  $11.19    $11.21</p>
<p> Silver (Kg)	 $156.37   $157.65</p>
<p> Platinum (t/oz)   $390.92   $377.26</p>
<p> Palladium (t/oz)  $138.43   $123.25</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
</text>
